  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The Clover – long pass to the corner, via the boards and a shot",
  "description": "Half court, one goal with a goalkeeper, groups of three. A stands with a ball in the centre circle, B at the centre line by the right boards and C in the right corner. A plays a long diagonal pass to C and immediately runs diagonally towards the shooting spot in the slot. At the same time B takes a few steps down the boards to get open. C passes to B, who plays it in to A, and A shoots first time.\n\nRotation: the shooter goes to B's spot, B to the corner and C to the centre circle. Switch sides after a few minutes.\n\nVariant: C first plays a wall pass with A on the way in, then passes to B. That adds one more pass before the shot and asks even more of the timing. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The long pass should be firm and stay on the floor."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "A: run straight after the pass – don't stop and watch."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "B: start down the boards when C receives the ball, not before."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Shoot first time off B's pass."
    }
  ],
